./leanncd/AGENTS.md:218:- **Fail loud, never silently drop semantics** — the intended convention across `DSL/` and `Eval/`: cyclic dataflow, non-injective scatters, nonlinear scatters, inconsistent scan axis orders, unsized axes are all explicit errors, not silent miscompiles or wrong answers. ⚠️ **Read this as "enforced where audited, aspirational where not."** This line previously stated the convention as achieved; the 2026-07-30 audit (`papers/semantic_payload_audit.md`) found **five past violations of it** — `evalScan` panicked on an unsized iteration axis instead of erroring, `brOpOfIdx` mapped any unknown tag to `.contract`, `writeSBr` swallowed CSV encode errors, `checkScatterNonlin` accepted `.recurMorphism` then discarded it, and (historically) `splitNonlins` dropped `rhs.agg`. Wave A closed six findings; **finding #6 (the boundary *decoder* defaults — `realizeStMat` zero-fill, `realizeBrBaseP`, `AcsetCodec`, `realizeSBr`) is still UNAUDITED.** The `splitNonlins` `agg`-drop entry is retained as accurate history — `splitNonlins` is now off-chain (regression-only helper in `Pipeline/Lowering.lean`; the production nonlinearity split happens at the `route` boundary via `physicalizeForRoute`), and the drop is provably vacuous even there (a non-sum `agg` statement has `nonlin = .identity` by construction, so the split never carries a droppable non-sum `agg`) — but it was a real bug at the time of the audit, and its lesson (a split that reconstructs a per-node body must carry every field of the source, not just the ones the split's arithmetic uses) still applies. Treat the convention as a goal to verify, not a guarantee to rely on.
