./leanncd/docs/test_portfolio.md:506:| EC15 | **per-term contraction scoping** `Y[i] := u[]·a[i] + W[i,k]·v[k]` | `k` appears only in the second term, so only that term is contracted over `k`; the `k`-less first term `u·a[i]` is added in exactly once | regression test for per-term (not whole-equation) contraction scoping. **Naming hazard:** a tensor/predicate named exactly `c` immediately followed by `[` (e.g. `c[k]`) fails to parse — not a DSL bug, but a **global token collision**: Mathlib's `Equiv.Perm` cycle notation (`Mathlib.GroupTheory.Perm.Cycle.Concrete`) registers `c[` as a single reserved token (`c[0,1,2]` = a permutation cycle), and Lean's tokenizer binds it greedily ahead of `ident` + `[`. Scoped to exactly the identifier `c` (`cc`, `c2`, uppercase `C` all parse fine). Avoid naming any tensor/predicate `c` in DSL programs | `[N]` `[E]` |
